{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Who filed matters here, and the driver filed. The driver's claim is a request to put a charge back — 'the $6.50 was taken back, please return my compensation'. The payments ledger shows the only line on this trip is a 6.50 SGD cancellation fee charged at 14:15:44 and reversed in full at 17:00:40 after the rider complained, leaving payment_status REFUNDED and refund_issued_sgd 6.50 (EV-FARE-05060; EV-TRIP-05060). Under POL-GEN-03 NO_ACTION is party-relative and 'never means restore a charge': the present state — rider not carrying the fee, fee withheld from the driver — is exactly what NO_ACTION preserves. The filing party's claim is a request for a charge to be reinstated, and the record contains no basis on which the rider should bear it again.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05060", "EV-TRIP-05060"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-22"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.payment_status and fare_breakdown.refund_issued_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The amount the driver seeks is not the amount the policy allows, and the rider said so on the record: her statement on file reads 'I was charged $6.50 for a no-show, more than the $5 I know about'. POL-NS-26 provides that the no-show fee 'is fixed at 5.00 SGD', and POL-NS-22 states the fee the policy authorises as 5.00 SGD. This rider was charged 6.50 SGD, 1.50 SGD above the schedule, and the ledger's own computation confirms it: policy_fee_sgd 5.00 against fee_charged_sgd 6.50, with fee_matches_policy false (EV-FARE-05060; EV-TRIP-05060). POL-NS-22 itself directs that where the record charged an amount other than 5.00 SGD the ruling acts on the amount charged and adds a referral naming that clause — that check has fired on this record, and the rider should not be left carrying a charge levied outside the fixed fee. The full reversal already on the ledger is the minimum correction of that overcharge and should not be disturbed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05060", "EV-TRIP-05060"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-22", "POL-NS-26"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.fee_charged_sgd and fare_breakdown.derived.money.policy_fee_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I do not contend the driver breached POL-NS-23, and I will not stretch the record: two in-app messages precede the cancellation (14:09:40 and 14:13:00) and one in-app call was placed at 14:12:10, unanswered, ringing 30 s, before the 14:15:40 cancellation, and the derived contact_before_cancel block marks the obligation met (EV-TRIP-05060; EV-CHAT-05060). Nor do I contend the free wait under POL-NS-21 had not run: cancellation came 385 s after the 14:09:15 arrival, past the 300 s free wait (EV-TRIP-05060). What that compliance buys the driver is the fee the schedule sets — 5.00 SGD — not the 6.50 SGD payment he asks for, and it does not cure the amount discrepancy on his own ledger.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05060", "EV-CHAT-05060"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23", "POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel.obligation_met and trip_record.derived.v7.free_wait.cancelled_after_free_wait",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the judge reaches the driver-no-show test, the fact that test needs cannot be fixed on this record: the trip is on-demand, scheduled_at is null, and the derived driver_deadline block returns deadline null with the reason 'on-demand trip: no scheduled time' (EV-TRIP-05060). POL-NS-24's own note directs that where the record carries no scheduled time and the deadline cannot be fixed, POL-GEN-26 applies: the case is escalated, no monetary outcome issues and the amount is held rather than released. Escalation on that footing leaves the rider not carrying the charge, which is the only outcome consistent with a record that cannot fix the deadline the clause runs on.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05060"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-24", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.driver_deadline.deadline",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The evidence package carries no traffic-data artifact for this trip at all: EV-ADVIS-05060-01 is MISSING, its issue code is MISSING_ARTIFACT, its weight is 0.0 and it carries no payload. Under POL-GEN-02(3) a MISSING artifact carries no fact, and under POL-GEN-26 no outcome is inferred from the absence of evidence. Any suggestion that conditions on the road excused or explained how the approach and the wait were handled therefore has nothing behind it in this record, and the driver's claim cannot be strengthened by material that was never attached.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05060-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on the rider's profile can be turned against her here. Rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d is 0, and even counting this trip it would be 1, below the 3 that POL-NS-25 requires before any flag; and POL-NS-25 is in any event a referral that never changes the ruling on the trip (EV-RPROF-05060). POL-GEN-01 confines profile material to the two named fields and the tests that name them, so the rider's history is not a ground for making her carry this fee — the amount question stays where the ledger puts it, at 5.00 SGD against a 6.50 SGD charge.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-05060", "EV-FARE-05060"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-25", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 6.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 6.5,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-22: the record charged 6.50 SGD for the no-show (EV-FARE-05060: fee_charged_sgd 6.50, policy_fee_sgd 5.00, fee_matches_policy false), an amount other than the 5.00 SGD no-show fee POL-NS-22 sets. Under POL-NS-22's final sentence the ruling acts on the amount charged and this referral names POL-NS-22, for platform review of the fee applied. Under POL-GEN-03 the referral does not suppress or alter the money."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the driver: your claim succeeds. To the rider: the fee you were refunded is restored to the driver, and the amount discrepancy you raised is referred, not used to void the fee.\n\nThe record is not disputed on the facts. This was an on-demand trip with no scheduled pickup time, so under POL-NS-21 the 5-minute (300 s) free wait ran from the driver's arrival, not from a booking time. The driver marked arrival at 14:09:15 (EV-TRIP-05060) and the GPS trace corroborates it: 25 fixes at 30 s intervals, 100% coverage, no gap over 30 s, nearest fix 2.9 m from the pickup at 14:09:55 with 4 m reported accuracy — inside the 50 m STANDARD-zone radius and the 25 m accuracy filter — and the trace then shows the vehicle stationary through the whole wait (EV-GPS-05060). The driver cancelled at 14:15:40, 385 s after arrival, 85 s past the 300 s free wait and after the record's own wait-timer expiry at 14:14:20. Before cancelling he sent two in-app messages (14:09:40 and 14:13:00) and placed one in-app call (14:12:10, unanswered, ringing 30 s), so POL-NS-23's contact obligation is met on both limbs. POL-NS-21 to POL-NS-23 are satisfied and the no-show fee stands.\n\nPOL-NS-22 therefore transfers the fee to the driver as compensation. The record charged 6.50 SGD where the policy fee is 5.00 SGD (EV-FARE-05060: policy_fee_sgd 5.00 against fee_charged_sgd 6.50, fee_matches_policy false; driver_compensation_if_upheld_sgd 6.50). POL-NS-22 directs that where the record charged an amount other than 5.00 SGD the ruling acts on the amount charged and adds a referral naming that clause, so the figure is 6.50 SGD and a POL-NS-22 referral is added. The ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION with both amount fields at 6.50 SGD — the same figure, being the money the ruling moves. The interim reversal of 17:00:40 that refunded the rider and withheld the fee from the driver is replaced.\n\nOn the rider's points. You do not deny the no-show, and your objection is the amount: 6.50 SGD against the 5.00 SGD you knew of. That is the discrepancy POL-NS-22's fee-amount check exists for, and it produces the referral above; it is not a ground for voiding the fee, and POL-GEN-03 provides that such a referral never suppresses the money. Your argument that NO_ACTION should leave the refund standing cannot succeed: POL-GEN-03 makes NO_ACTION party-relative and says it never means 'restore a charge', so the driver's request cannot be answered with NO_ACTION; where the fee stands the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION. Your POL-NS-24 / POL-GEN-26 escalation point does not open: the record establishes when the driver arrived and that he did reach and hold the pickup (EV-TRIP-05060 and EV-GPS-05060), and POL-NS-21 itself supplies the on-demand timing, so no fact any operative rule needs is missing; in any event POL-NS-24 could not change the outcome, since the rider already holds the refund and no 5.00 SGD goodwill credit is due, because contact was attempted. The absent traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-05060-01, MISSING, weight 0.0) carries no fact per POL-GEN-02(3), and nothing here turns on road conditions. Your profile point is right and changes nothing: the POL-NS-25 counter is absent and, even counting this trip, the count is 1, below 3, so no repeat no-show referral arises.\n\nThere is no safety flag (POL-GEN-21) and no fraud flag on either profile, so the 0.95 confidence rule is not engaged; the value is 6.50 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's first band, so under POL-NS-26 this AI ruling is final. My confidence is 0.95, within the 1.0 carried by every artifact that decides the case — EV-TRIP-05060, EV-GPS-05060, EV-CHAT-05060 and EV-FARE-05060, all at weight 1.0 — and no artifact relied on falls below 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 6.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 6.5,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-22: the record charged SGD 6.50 for this no-show, not the fixed SGD 5.00 fee (fee_charged_sgd 6.50 against policy_fee_sgd 5.00, fee_matches_policy false) — the fee-amount discrepancy is referred for review; per POL-GEN-03 it does not suppress the money the ruling moves."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the driver: your no-show cancellation was validly carried out, so the fee stands and the ruling goes your way. Because TRP-05060 was on-demand, POL-NS-21 runs the 300 s free wait from your arrival; you marked arrived at 14:09:15 and cancelled at 14:15:40, 385 s later, past the wait (EV-TRIP-05060, wait_timer_expired 14:14:20). The GPS trace corroborates the arrival (EV-GPS-05060): nearest fix 2.89 m from the pickup with 4 m reported accuracy, well inside the STANDARD 50 m arrival radius and the 25 m accuracy filter, and speed 0 from 14:09:25 to 14:15:25. Your POL-NS-23 contact obligation is met on both limbs — messages at 14:09:40 and 14:13:00 (EV-CHAT-05060) and a call placed at 14:12:10 (EV-TRIP-05060) — all before the 14:15:40 cancellation, so no FULL_REFUND arises. POL-NS-22 accordingly makes the ruling DRIVER_COMPENSATION. However, the ledger charged 6.50 SGD, not the 5.00 SGD the clause fixes (EV-FARE-05060: fee_charged_sgd 6.50, policy_fee_sgd 5.00, fee_matches_policy false). POL-NS-22 directs that where the record charged an amount other than 5.00 SGD the ruling acts on the amount charged and adds a referral naming that clause, so both money fields carry 6.50 SGD and the POL-NS-22 referral above accompanies the ruling; POL-GEN-03 confirms a referral never suppresses the money.\n\nTo the rider: both of your points are answered. First, POL-NS-24 cannot give you a free cancellation here and does not send this case to a human reviewer. It asks whether the driver arrived later than the scheduled pickup time plus 5 minutes, and this on-demand trip has no scheduled pickup time at all (trip_record.scheduled_at is null; the derived driver_deadline block returns deadline null for that reason). The test has no schedule to run against, finds nothing qualifying, and no goodwill credit follows (the driver attempted contact in any case). POL-GEN-26 does not open either: every fact the operative rules need — when the driver arrived, how long he waited, and whether he messaged and called before cancelling — is carried by COMPLETE artifacts at weight 1.0 (EV-TRIP-05060, EV-GPS-05060, EV-CHAT-05060), so nothing is missing or impaired. The single absent artifact, EV-ADVIS-05060-01 (MISSING, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT), is a traffic advisory that carries no fact under POL-GEN-02(3) and that no operative rule needs. Second, your point about the amount is well taken but does not void the fee: the 6.50 SGD charged exceeds the 5.00 SGD fixed fee, and that is precisely what POL-NS-22's fee-amount check addresses — it produces the referral, not a refund. NO_ACTION is rejected: the driver's claim is supported on this record, and the 17:00:40 reversal was an interim measure taken pending review, not a final determination.\n\nOn the profiles and confidence: neither profile carries a fraud flag (rider_profile.fraud_flags 0, driver_profile.fraud_flags 0), so POL-GEN-22's 0.95 requirement is not engaged; with a dispute value of 6.50 SGD this is an AI-final no-show under POL-NS-26. No POL-NS-25 flag arises: rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d is not present on this record, and POL-NS-25 (C7) applies only where that counter is present. Confidence 0.9: every artifact carrying the deciding facts — EV-TRIP-05060, EV-GPS-05060, EV-CHAT-05060 and EV-FARE-05060 — is at weight 1.0, so the cap is 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
